(The other 25 forms {[aeiou]'[aeiou]} with apostrophes in them will all
be 'approved' as cmene and aren't interesting to show.)  I think the
'special' cases above are that iy and uy are allowed in cmene, but other
pairs involving {y} are not allowed.  That was my reading of the book
anyway.  I think we established some time back that any cluster involving
just a,e,i,o or u was allowed in cmene and fu'ivla (although for fu'ivla
the consonant structure must not match that of a lujvo or gismu.)

Are there any systematic faults in this analysis?  If there are, please
